      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T09:38:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Therefore these services are then disabled for the image of that specific device type to make it lighter (the service is removed from the device\u0027s image).\n\nWhat is returned from `Context.getSystemService(MediaSessionManager.class)` on such a device? It seems it should return `null`, in which case I think nobody should be invoking these methods (because they can\u0027t get an instance of `MediaSessionManager` to invoke them on - so there\u0027s no need for the null checking at this level? \n\nApologies if we don\u0027t fully understand the problem you\u0027re solving here - but until we do so (perhaps by filing the partner issue suggested above), I\u0027m afraid we are unlikely to approve this change.",
